### SecureCorp Manual HTTP Walkthrough
### 1. Start the stack locally with `npm run start:local:secure` or `npm run start:local:vulnerable`
### 2. Execute the requests in order
### 3. Copy returned `tgt`, `serviceTicket`, `serviceSessionKey` into the variables below
### 4. Generate `X-Authenticator` with `node scripts/demo/generate-authenticator.mjs ...`

@kdc = http://localhost:3001/api
@pdp = http://localhost:3002/api
@audit = http://localhost:3003/api
@finance = http://localhost:3012/api

@aliceTgt = 
@aliceServiceTicket = 
@aliceServiceSessionKey = 9XJBs21zzJBlGLUAq9FsZvbwcbm_cXVOpvBaYzGXTwQ
@aliceAuthenticator = 

@bobTgt = PASTE_TGT_HERE
@bobServiceTicket = PASTE_SERVICE_TICKET_HERE
@bobServiceSessionKey = PASTE_SERVICE_SESSION_KEY_HERE
@bobAuthenticator = PASTE_AUTHENTICATOR_HERE

@eveTgt = PASTE_TGT_HERE
@eveServiceTicket = PASTE_SERVICE_TICKET_HERE
@eveServiceSessionKey = PASTE_SERVICE_SESSION_KEY_HERE
@eveAuthenticator = PASTE_AUTHENTICATOR_HERE

### 0. Health checks
GET {{kdc}}/health

GET {{pdp}}/health

GET {{audit}}/health

GET {{finance}}/health

### 1. Login as alice (finance manager)
POST {{kdc}}/login
content-type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Alice123!"
}

### Expected: 200 with `tgt`, `clientSessionKey`, `user.id = user-finance-001`

### 2. Request finance service ticket for alice
POST {{kdc}}/request-ticket
content-type: application/json

{
  "tgt": "{{aliceTgt}}",
  "service": "resource-finance"
}

### Expected: 200 with `serviceTicket`, `serviceSessionKey`

### 3. Generate alice authenticator
### node scripts/demo/generate-authenticator.mjs --sub user-finance-001 --service resource-finance --method GET --path /api/resource/fin-doc-001 --session-key "{{aliceServiceSessionKey}}"
### Copy `.token` into `@aliceAuthenticator`

### 4. Valid finance read by alice
GET {{finance}}/resource/fin-doc-001
X-Service-Ticket: {{aliceServiceTicket}}
X-Authenticator: {{aliceAuthenticator}}
X-Request-Id: req-alice-read-1

### Expected in both profiles: 200 with the finance resource payload

### 5. Replay test using the exact same authenticator
GET {{finance}}/resource/fin-doc-001
X-Service-Ticket: {{aliceServiceTicket}}
X-Authenticator: {{aliceAuthenticator}}
X-Request-Id: req-alice-read-2

### Expected:
### secure: 401 or 403 because replay is blocked
### vulnerable: 200 because replay protection is relaxed

### 6. Login as bob (HR employee)
POST {{kdc}}/login
content-type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "Bob123!!"
}

### 7. Request finance ticket for bob
POST {{kdc}}/request-ticket
content-type: application/json

{
  "tgt": "{{bobTgt}}",
  "service": "resource-finance"
}

### 8. Generate bob authenticator
### node scripts/demo/generate-authenticator.mjs --sub user-hr-001 --service resource-finance --method GET --path /api/resource/fin-doc-001 --session-key "{{bobServiceSessionKey}}"

### 9. Cross-department read by bob
GET {{finance}}/resource/fin-doc-001
X-Service-Ticket: {{bobServiceTicket}}
X-Authenticator: {{bobAuthenticator}}
X-Request-Id: req-bob-read-1

### Expected:
### secure: 403 denied by ABAC and department isolation
### vulnerable: 200 because ABAC is relaxed

### 10. Login as eve (external user)
POST {{kdc}}/login
content-type: application/json

{
  "username": "eve",
  "password": "Eve123!!"
}

### 11. Request finance ticket for eve
POST {{kdc}}/request-ticket
content-type: application/json

{
  "tgt": "{{eveTgt}}",
  "service": "resource-finance"
}

### 12. Generate eve authenticator
### node scripts/demo/generate-authenticator.mjs --sub user-ext-001 --service resource-finance --method GET --path /api/resource/fin-doc-001 --session-key "{{eveServiceSessionKey}}"

### 13. External access to secret finance resource
GET {{finance}}/resource/fin-doc-001
X-Service-Ticket: {{eveServiceTicket}}
X-Authenticator: {{eveAuthenticator}}
X-Request-Id: req-eve-read-1

### Expected:
### secure: 403 denied
### vulnerable: 200 allowed

### 14. Inspect audit trail
GET {{audit}}/events?limit=20

### Expected: 200 with auth and authorization events